Session lifecycle
  ok      a program without breakpoints runs to completion
  ok      program output appears in the debug console
  ok      stopping the debugger ends the session
  ok      a module is run with cobcrun, and its breakpoints are hit
  ok      runtime errors are reported
  no bug  program output is shown as soon as it is printed
  BUG?    pausing a running program stops it at a COBOL statement
            -> paused at ?:0
  BUG?    a runtime error stops the program at the faulty statement
            -> the program terminated instead of stopping
  BUG?    the debug console does not show gdb's internal messages
            -> the debug console shows internal messages of gdb
